  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Wpcrl/1341/2024 on 11 December, 2024 202 Office N ot e s, r e por t s, or de r s or pr oce e din gs Sl. Date or dir e ct ions Court'S Or Jud Ge'S Ord Er S N o. a nd Re gist r a r 's or de r w it h Signa t ur e s WPCRL No. 1341 of 2024 U Hon'ble Manoj Kumar Tiwari, A.C.J. U Hon'ble Pankaj Purohit, J. Mr. Lokendra Dobhal, Advocate for petitioner and S.S. Chauhan, Deputy Advocate General assisted by Mr. R.K. Joshi, Brief Holder for State of Uttarakhand.",
    "facts": "3. According to petitioner, he was issued a license for running a grocery shop by Department of Food Safety, Government of Uttarakhand and he was also issued a license for retail sale of foreign liquor by Excise Department on 25.10.2024. It is further stated that a composite grocery and liquor shop has to be run from a rented accommodation, which he has taken on lease for a period of 5 years. The grievance raised by petitioner is that respondent Nos. 7, 8, 9 & 10 and some other persons residing in the locality are not permitting petitioner to run his business for which he has been issued license by competent authority.",
    "arguments": "6. Learned counsel for petitioner, on instructions, submitted that petitioner do not intend to run massage parlour and he gave an undertaking on behalf of his client that no massage parlour will ever be run from the premises in question."
  },
